[2026/07/08 15:38:57] [DEBUG] isgsa.nodeAgent: Review summary: **Bug: Repeated interactions in Last.FM dataset cause Dataset building to fail.**

The error occurs in `load_and_preprocess_lastfm()` at line 206:
```
dataset = from_interactions_df(df, rating_col="rating", timestamp_col="timestamp")
```

The LensKit error message says: `found 110798 forbidden repeat interactions (of 173778)` — more than half of the interactions are duplicate (user, item) pairs. This is because the HetRec Last.FM dataset uses `user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat` which records when a user tagged an artist. Users can tag the same artist multiple times, producing repeated (user, item) interactions. Since `from_interactions_df` internally sets `allow_repeats=False` (as seen in the source code), LensKit rejects these duplicates.

**Fix:** The Last.FM data should be deduplicated before building the dataset. There are two approaches:

1. **Simple deduplication (preferred):** Drop duplicate (user_id, item_id) pairs before passing to `from_interactions_df`. Since this is implicit feedback, keeping only one interaction per user-item pair makes sense:
   ```python
   df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=["user_id", "item_id"])
   ```

2. **Alternative using DatasetBuilder directly:** Use `DatasetBuilder` with `allow_repeats=True` and `remove_repeats=True` parameters to handle repeats automatically.

The simplest fix is approach #1 — add `df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=["user_id", "item_id"])` right before the `from_interactions_df()` call in `load_and_preprocess_lastfm()`. This preserves the implicit feedback nature (rating=1) while removing duplicate entries that confuse the framework.
